<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Venetia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Venetia is a historical region of north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleonic-wars">Napoleonic Wars</a> it was ruled by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austrian-empire">Austrian Empire</a> as part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-lombardy-venetia">Kingdom of Lombardy–Venetia</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austro-Hungarian Empire</a> profile notes that defeat in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-prussian-war">Austro-Prussian War</a> of 1866 stripped <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> of Venetia, contributing to the reconstitution of the empire in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-compromise-of-1867">Compromise of 1867</a>.</p></div>
